meta {
  name: Update Sold Deal (Before Quote)
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sold-deals/{{createdSoldDealId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  { "soldDate": "2026-01-20" }
}

tests {
  test("rejects a sale dated before the quote it was sold from", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(400);
    expect(res.getBody().message).to.contain("Sold date cannot be before the quote date (2026-02-01)");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /sold-deals/:id — a sale cannot precede its quote (PAC-159 §1b)

  The deal was sold from the recap the Quote Recaps folder re-dated to
  **2026-02-01** (`Deal.quoteRecapId`), so 2026-01-20 is refused. The pair is
  the deal and **its** recap only: a lead can hold several quotes and several
  deals, and a requote after the first sale is legitimate. A deal with no
  linked recap (every migrated deal) is checked against no quote. Same day is
  allowed — quoted and sold on one visit is normal.
}
